<title>JAPAN: Japanese firms see no impact from Boeing merger.</title>
<headline>Japanese firms see no impact from Boeing merger.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese aircraft makers and airlines said on Monday that the planned merger of Boeing Co and McDonnell Douglas Corp was unlikely to affect their business.</p>
<p>Japan's largest aircraft maker, Mitsubishi Heavy Industries Ltd, said it did not expect its relationship with Boeing to be much affected by the planned merger.</p>
<p>&quot;We need to closely watch the merger, but unless Boeing and McDonnell Douglas change their existing policies, we believe there will be no major impact on our relationship,&quot; Mitsubishi Heavy Industries said in a statement.</p>
</text>
